hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"339","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawrqi and Muammal bin Hisham Al-Yashkari told us, saying: Ibn Ulayya told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq. H Al-Fadl bin Yaqoub Al-Jazari narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul-Ala, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, Yazid bin Abi Habib narrated to me, on the authority of Marthad bin Abdullah Al-Yazani said: Abu Ayyub came to us as a conqueror, and Uqba bin Amir was in charge of Egypt at that time, so he delayed sunset, so he rose to it. Abu Ayyub said: What is this prayer, O Uqba? He said: We were busy, and he said: By God, my only problem is for people to think that you saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, doing this. I heard The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “My nation will continue to be well or on the right path, as long as they do not delay sunset until the stars clash.” This is the wording of the hadith of Al-Dawraqi, and Al-Ma’mal and Al-Fadl ibn Ya’qub said: Did you not hear the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “My nation will not cease to exist. On the authority of Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi, on the authority of Ziyad ibn Abdullah, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Yazid ibn Abi Habib: He mentioned the hadith and said: As for Did you hear the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “My nation will continue to be well or according to its fitrah unless they delay sunset until the stars collide?” He said: Yes"
"340","On the authority of Abu Zur’ah, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Musa, on the authority of Abbad ibn Al-Awwam, on the authority of Omar ibn Ibrahim, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Al-Ahnaf ibn Qays, on the authority of Al-Abbas ibn Abdul-Muttalib, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “My nation will continue to break the fast, as long as they do not delay sunset until \The stars collide.\"" Abu Bakr said: His saying: “My nation will continue to be well"","" as long as they do not delay sunset until the stars collide"",""” is an indication that his saying in Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas reported: It is sunset time unless the twilight bull falls. He only wanted a time of excuse and necessity"","" not to do it intentionally. Delaying the Maghrib prayer until twilight approaches"","" because the clash of stars occurs a long time before twilight sets"","" in which it is possible to pray After the clash of the stars"","" before the twilight disappears"","" many rak’ahs"","" more than four rak’ahs"""""
